<div>
    <p>One row per <code>BonusTypeEnum</code> case (registration/purchase/review/manual). For <code>purchase</code>, <code>amount</code> is ignored — the actual award is the sum of each order line's <code>ShopProduct.bonuses * quantity</code>, computed by <code>OrderService::addOrderBonuses()</code> when an order's status reaches <code>delivered</code>. <code>delay_days</code>/<code>validity_days</code> still apply to every type, including purchase.</p>
    <p><code>registration</code>/<code>manual</code> are ported in <code>BonusService</code> but not wired to anything yet — registration has no hook point without touching the core Auth package, and manual adjustment never had an admin action even in the source project. <code>review</code> is wired: <code>ReviewObserver</code> calls <code>ReviewService::addBonusesForReview()</code> on every review create/update, which awards it once per verified completed purchase of that product.</p>
    <p>Schedule <code>php artisan bonuses:activate</code> and <code>php artisan bonuses:expire</code> (e.g. daily) to move transactions through their pending → available → expired lifecycle — neither runs automatically.</p>
</div>
